 roughly with the market, though its beta has shifted (1y 0.10 vs 5y 0.90), so read it loosely.","About $46.6M trades a day, enough to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 62% in the 2020 crash, 30% in the 2022 bear market and 88% in 2008."],"val":["The stock trades 51% below its blended-model fair value of $402, a meaningful margin of safety.","The fair-value models corroborate one another (dispersion 12%).","On multiples it looks cheap against Consumer Cyclical peers: P/E 7.8 vs 18.8 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 1% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are attractive: an EBIT/EV of 9.7% (vs the 8% bar).","The 11 covering analysts target $225 on average, 14% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 11% earns above the cost of capital of 8.1%, but the 3pp spread is short of the 7pp moat bar; returns have been steady (CV 0.25).","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.58x.","ROE of 13% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (3.0x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.2% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 3.3x net debt to EBITDA ($104.7M of cash against $3.1B of debt), with interest covered 3.1x.","The current ratio of 0.95 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 5.3% over 3 years, 20.3% over 5 years and 10.6% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 30%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 8%.","Capex runs 2.1x depreciation (1.0% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.9%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insider trading is two-way: 4 purchases and 1 sale over the past year, net $919K bought.","Shareholder yield is a modest 0.4% (0.4% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 1.5% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","Short interest is elevated at 12.4% of the float, 3.8 days to cover."],"people":["With about 15,000 employees, each generates about $1.2M of revenue, 3.1x the Consumer Cyclical median, and revenue has grown 10.8% a year across its filed history.","CEO pay is $1.8M (1x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (3/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $2K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":68,"head":"Invest: trades 51% below fair value of $402; revenue grew 20.3%/yr over 5y.","pros":["Composite 45, above the 39 line (gates 13/26)","Trades 51% below fair value of $402","Revenue grew 20.3%/yr over 5y","P/E 7.8x vs sector 18.8x","Insiders net buyers ($919K over 12 months)"],"cons":["Net debt/EBITDA 3.3x","12-1 month momentum -26%"],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":341.64,"vc":{"base":401.93,"base_src":"blend","bear":null,"bull":null,"alt_median":401.93,"n_alt":2,"gap":null,"dispersion":0.1222,"level":"MEDIUM","why":[]},"med":{"pe":18.8184,"ev_ebitda":10.707,"pfcf":16.6971,"pb":2.3,"roic":0.1268,"gross_margin":0.346,"fcf_margin":0.0621,"div_yield":0.0232}},"ticker":"ABG","date":"2026-11-13"}